Revised row set for F2 (post version): 69 rows. The matcher lists 68 numeral units; the 69th row is 'tens' (node 79), a unit the matcher missed and the checker found. 43 rows are figures: 28 reproduced, 11 log-only, 2 discrepant, 2 not found. The other 26 are not figures: axis ticks, the iso-d′ reference levels, the [g3-B] identifier, a citation year, model-name labels and 'two series'.

All six checker findings were verified against their cited lines and accepted; none was rejected. The substantive one reverses a span note. This F2 carries no d′, c or Fisher-p annotations, which block :34 directs for the post version and note v0.3 :13 and :3 say it has. Its metadata date (2026-10-06) predates the block (bbc9ffe, 2026-10-07) and N2's ROC JSON (09c3a8c, 2026-10-08), so it is the Digest-seat draft, and N1's pass does not cover an annotated F2. That goes to the PI: re-render with d′/c/p and run a new N1 pass, or reword note :13 and :3.

Our own figures all reproduce: the exploration points and counts, the criterion markers and decidable range, the greedy zeros, and 'our tens' (24, 48 and 96 trials run per stage; N2 :136). The Macar base, SFT and DPO rates are log-only. Watch-list status:
- W3 fires twice (nodes 46 and 73). The Instruct FPR is plotted at 0.003 against v1's 0.000; on Code's transcription reading it is corrected, otherwise it is a STOP. Note v0.3 writes the same value as '0–0.003' (:92, :208), so F2 and the note must be changed together.
- W5 fires at node 79. '~800/~80 per stage' is presented as the source's n without its premise, so it is not found (L032); the cause is now worded as an ambiguous unit rather than a wrong one. If the sentence is restated rather than cut, the 'against our tens' contrast fails on the control side for the criterion arm (96 > ~80).
- W4 at node 40 is a value collision (source base TPR, L037).
- The other watch items are absent from F2.

The N2(ii) STOP stays active on F2's greedy series (nodes 24-25 and 47-50). Note v0.3 :3 and :209 call it resolved by a rewording that F2 does not carry.

F2 also omits several dispositions routed to it:
- the base non-asserting disclosure;
- FLAG-3's 0.176 beside SFT;
